Day 28 – Graph Cycle Detection
Problems Solved
Detect Cycle in Undirected Graph (DFS)
Detect Cycle in Directed Graph (DFS + Path Tracking)
Key Concepts
Graph Traversal
Depth First Search (DFS)
Parent Node Tracking
Recursion Stack / Path Set
Cycle Detection
Learning Summary
Undirected Graph

Cycle exists when:

A neighbour is already visited
The neighbour is not the parent node

Used:

DFS
Parent Tracking

Time Complexity: O(V + E)

Directed Graph

Cycle exists when:

During DFS, a neighbour is found in the current recursion path

Used:

DFS
Visited Set
Path Set (Recursion Stack)

Time Complexity: O(V + E)

Biggest Takeaway

Although both problems are about cycle detection, the logic differs significantly:

Undirected Graph → Parent Check
Directed Graph → Recursion Path Check
